=Consonant:
Consonant cluster: group of consonants without vowel
Liquid consonant: more often part of consonant clusters and syllable nucleus [RL]

Obstruent: block airflow, plosives + fricatives + affricates
Sonorant: continuous airflow, voiced, vowels + nasals + liquids

=Finite verb: complements subject, with grammatical categories
=Nonfinite verb: without grammatical categories
Infinitive: basic dictionary form
Participle: function as adjective
Gerund: function as noun

#
Morphology: how words are formed
Syntax: how words form sentences
Semantics: meaning of words

#
Grammatical categories

=Grammatical number: singular, plural
=Grammatical person: 1st (speaker), 2nd (spoken to), 3rd (others)
=Grammatical gender: masculine, feminine, neuter

=Grammatical tense: time reference
Present tense: now
Preterite: past
- german: written
- spanish: completed
- english: completed and specific time
Perfect: past
- german: spoken
- spanish: ongoing
- english: ongoing or no exact time
Future: expectation

=Grammatical mood: modality
Indicative: factual
Conditional: if then
Subjunctive: hypothetical
Imperative: command

=Grammatical voice: relationship between action and subject
Active: subject does action
Passive: action done to subject

=Grammatical aspect: duration over time
Perfective: once
Imperfective: continuous / habitual

